Notes on a few deliberate design decisions (all covered by the tests above): `stock_at` returns `0` for known sku/location pairs that simply have no stock row yet; failed rule checks happen before any mutation, so a rejected operation changes nothing on disk or in memory; `adjust` records the signed delta in `qty` with the affected location in `src`; and a same-location transfer is permitted (it is a no-op for occupancy, so the destination capacity check is skipped for `src == dst`).
